\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Walk attention marks in Bob Mac Capture's idle agenda[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Whenever the Obsidian walker selector shows attention for a family [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim](an off-family dot or selected-family ink) — `s` review, `w` lanes,[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]`b` bank — Bob Mac Capture's idle agenda shows that family's mark [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim](its letter with a hue dot) at the title row's trailing edge, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]computed by bob from the same contract, and shows nothing [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]otherwise.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]3[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]mac_walk_attention_marks.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202611/mac_walk_attention_marks.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-mx[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-mx/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Freshness scan parses the vault once[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]scan-once[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]scan-once: share one Tasks settings read and one TaskIndex across the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]freshness scan's READY/PENDING/NEXT/OPEN queries and its all-task pass, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with byte-identical outputs and recorded before/after timings.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]bob walks attention report and contract[/bold #D7AFFF]                       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]bob-walks[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]bob-walks: add the read-only `bob walks` command (human + JSON schema 1)[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]that reports s/w/b attention with per-family failure isolation, plus the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs/walks.md contract, conformance vectors, goldens, and doc updates.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Pin the walker footer to the walks conformance vectors[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]plugin-parity[dim] · [dim][/dim]after bob-walks[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]plugin-parity: run the docs/walks.md vectors against bob-ledger-tools' [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]real attention pushes in a JS test, fix any drift in favor of the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]contract, link the contract from the plugin docs, and sync.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]CaptureCore walks models, client, tones, and presentation[/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]mac-walks-core[dim] · [dim][/dim]after bob-walks[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]mac-walks-core: decode `bob walks --format json` on its own process [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]lane, add the tier hue table, title-row walk marks in the agenda [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]presentation, the pure refresh policy, fake-bob support, protocol docs, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and green macOS CI.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Walk marks store, view, docs, and decision record[/bold #D7AFFF]             [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]mac-walk-marks[dim] · [dim][/dim]after mac-walks-core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]mac-walk-marks: wire the walks store and refresh triggers, paint the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]marks at the title row's trailing edge with motion, contrast, and 